Short:        Self-hosted cloud: drive, sync, client
Author:       Ronny Krueger
Uploader:     amitools@planet-rk.de (Ronny Krueger)
Type:         comm/net
Version:      @VERSION@
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.0.0
Requires:     util/libs/AmiSSL-v5-OS3.lha; util/libs/mui38usr.lha
Distribution: Aminet

AmiCloud connects your Amiga to your own AmiCloud server over HTTPS.
Files can be used from the command line (amicloud), an interactive shell
(amicloud-shell), a two-pane MUI file manager (amicloud-commander), a
folder sync tool (amicloud-sync) or simply as the DOS volume AMICLOUD:
provided by a filesystem handler. AmiCloudPrefs edits the settings.

The server (PHP 7.4+, MariaDB/MySQL) is included: the drawer Server
holds AmiCloud-Server-@VERSION@.tar.gz with its installation guide.

Installation
------------
Unpack the archive and double-click "Install-AmiCloud" (Commodore
Installer, part of OS 3.2 in SYS:System). Without the Installer, use the
shell script instead:  CD AmiCloud  and  Execute Install-AmiCloud.shell
Existing settings and an existing DOSDriver are never overwritten.

Requirements
------------
- AmigaOS 3.x, 68020 or better (since 0.2), no FPU needed
- a TCP/IP stack with bsdsocket.library (Roadshow, AmiTCP, Miami, ...)
- AmiSSL 5 (Aminet util/libs/AmiSSL-v5-OS3.lha)
- MUI 3.8 or newer for amicloud-commander only (util/libs/mui38usr.lha)
- optional: codesets.library 6 or newer for umlauts in other charsets
  than ISO-8859-1 (util/libs/codesets-6.22.lha)
- optional: xvs.library for the virus check of downloads
  (util/virus/xvslibrary.lha)
- an AmiCloud server (included, see the drawer Server)

Status
------
Experimental software, developed with the help of Claude (an AI
assistant by Anthropic) and written primarily for the author's own use.
Try it with copies of your data first; use at your own risk.

Documentation and user interface are in German.
Die Dokumentation (Docs/AmiCloud.guide) und die Programme sind deutsch.

